    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0578" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1491: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton (Ballantine) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-11T11:00:00+08:00">March 11, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 12—7:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My February 26, 4 p.m.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d498-f1"/> I have been informed by
                    the military authorities that on account of the approach of the Kwantung forces
                        <pb facs="0579" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/> the Communists have raised the
                    siege of Kanchow, and that while Americans there are presumably safe it will be
                    impossible to confirm this until the Kwantung forces reach there.</p>
                <p>Legation, Nanking, Hankow and Department informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ballantine</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
